1
00:07:54,000 --> 00:08:00,000
He came from nothing. He conquered everything.

2
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Napoleon is a history, war, romance film directed by Ridley Scott.

3
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:48,000
An epic that details the checkered rise and fall of French Emperor Napoleon Bonaparte and his relentless
journey to power through the prism of his addictive, volatile relationship with his wife, Josephine.

4
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Napoleon Bonaparte, played by Joaquin Phoenix.

5
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:36,000
Josephine Bonaparte, played by Vanessa Kirby.

6
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:30,000
Paul Barras, played by Tahar Rahim.

7
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:24,000
Duke of Wellington, played by Rupert Everett.

8
01:03:12,000 --> 01:03:18,000
Junot, played by Mark Bonnar.

9
01:11:06,000 --> 01:11:12,000
Talleyrand, played by Paul Rhys.

10
01:19:00,000 --> 01:19:06,000
Napoleon is a 2023 epic historical war film directed and co-produced
by Ridley Scott from a screenplay by David Scarpa.

11
01:26:54,000 --> 01:27:00,000
Based on the life of Napoleon and primarily depicting his rise to power, as well as his relationship with
his wife, Joséphine, it stars Joaquin Phoenix as Napoleon and Vanessa Kirby as Joséphine.

12
01:34:48,000 --> 01:34:54,000
In October 2020, Scott announced Napoleon as his next project.

13
01:42:42,000 --> 01:42:48,000
Following delays and recastings due to the COVID-19 pandemic, filming
began in February 2022 in England, lasting several months.

14
01:50:36,000 --> 01:50:42,000
In addition to writer David Scarpa, frequent Scott collaborators included
cinematographer Dariusz Wolski and editor Claire Simpson.

15
01:58:30,000 --> 01:58:36,000
Napoleon premiered at Salle Pleyel in Paris on November 14, 2023, and was released in the United States and United Kingdom on
November 22 by Columbia Pictures (via Sony Pictures Releasing) before streaming on Apple TV+ on March 1, 2024.

16
02:06:24,000 --> 02:06:30,000
The film grossed $222.4 million worldwide and received mixed reviews from critics, who praised the battle sequences
and performances but criticized its uneven tone, rushed pacing, and lack of historical accuracy.

17
02:14:18,000 --> 02:14:24,000
At the 96th Academy Awards, the film received nominations for Best
Production Design, Best Costume Design, and Best Visual Effects.

18
02:22:12,000 --> 02:22:18,000
The film explores themes of empire, france,
general, biography, napoleon bonaparte.

19
02:30:06,000 --> 02:30:12,000
The tone is emotional.
